10
01:17:46,666 --> 01:17:52,666
Rosewood is a 1997 American historical drama film directed by John Singleton, inspired by the 1923
Rosewood massacre in Florida, when a white mob killed black people and destroyed their town.

11
01:25:33,333 --> 01:25:39,333
It stars Ving Rhames as an outsider who comes into Rosewood and inspires
residents to self-defense, wielding his pistols in a fight.

12
01:33:20,000 --> 01:33:26,000
The supporting cast includes Don Cheadle as Sylvester Carrier, a resident who was a witness, defender of his family and
victim of the riot; and Jon Voight as John Wright, a sympathetic White store owner who lives in Rosewood.

13
01:41:06,666 --> 01:41:12,666
The three characters become entangled in an attempt to save people from
racist White people attacking the Black residents of Rosewood.

14
01:48:53,333 --> 01:48:59,333
Despite generally favorable reviews, the film was not a commercial success and
was unable to recoup its $17 million budget at the box office.

15
01:56:40,000 --> 01:56:46,000
The film was entered into the 47th Berlin International Film Festival.

16
02:04:26,666 --> 02:04:32,666
The film explores themes of small town, sheriff, racial
segregation, based on true story, race riot.

17
02:12:13,333 --> 02:12:19,333
The tone is emotional and intense.
